{"paper": "CHSL-Tier1-10-Jul-2024-Shift3.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "sequential", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 25, "tagged_count": 25, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "English", "added": false}, {"text": "Math", "added": false}, {"text": "Economics", "added": false}, {"text": "Science", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 2, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "88.15%", "added": false}, {"text": "76.53%", "added": false}, {"text": "81.21%", "added": false}, {"text": "80.12%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 3, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 4, "text": "A cuboid with dimensions 20cm, 12cm, and 10 cm is cut into 8 identical pieces by 3 cuts. What will be the total surface area of all the pieces?", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cube-cuboid", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 5, "text": "An article is of size 9 cm × 6 cm × 3 cm. The number of such articles that can be packed in a box measuring 63 cm × 42 cm × 21 cm is:", "options": [{"text": "343", "added": false}, {"text": "243", "added": false}, {"text": "49", "added": false}, {"text": "196", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 6, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 7, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 8, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 9, "text": "Chords AB and CD of a circle, when produced, meet at a point P outside the circle. If AB = 6 cm, CD = 3 cm and PD = 5 cm, then PB is equal to:", "options": [{"text": "9 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "8 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "4 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "6 cm", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "tangents-and-chords", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 10, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "₹1,500, 12%", "added": false}, {"text": "₹1,200, 10%", "added": false}, {"text": "₹1,500, 15%", "added": false}, {"text": "₹1,200, 12%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 11, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 12, "text": "With a uniform speed, a car covers a distance in 16 hours. Had the speed been increased by 20 km/h, the same distance would have been covered in 12 hours. The total distance covered by the car is:", "options": [{"text": "720 km", "added": false}, {"text": "1080 km", "added": false}, {"text": "960 km", "added": false}, {"text": "480 km", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "basic-tsd", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 13, "text": "The centres of two circles of radii 20 cm and 32 cm are 60 cm apart. What is the ratio of the length of the direct common tangent to the length of the transverse common tangent to these circles?", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "tangents-and-chords", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 14, "text": "In a triangle PQR, RS intersects PQ at point S. The sides of the triangle QR = 36 cm, SQ = 27 cm, RS = 18 cm and ∠ QRS = ∠ QPR. What is the ratio of the perimeter of ∆PRS to that of ∆QSR?", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 2D", "sub": "triangle-and-quadrilaterals", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 15, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 16, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 17, "text": "If 42 ÷ 3 + k × 3 – 22 ÷ 11 + 4 = 28, then the value of k is:", "options": [{"text": "0", "added": false}, {"text": "1", "added": false}, {"text": "4", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 18, "text": "In an election, a candidate secures 40% of the votes, but is defeated by the only other candidate with a majority of 298 votes. Find the total number of votes recorded.", "options": [{"text": "1,470", "added": false}, {"text": "1,270", "added": false}, {"text": "1,490", "added": false}, {"text": "1,290", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "basic-percentage", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 19, "text": "The sides AB and AC of △ ABC are produced to points D and E, respectively. The bisectors of ∠ CBD and ∠ BCE meet at P. If ∠ A = 72°, then the measure of ∠ P is:", "options": [{"text": "55°", "added": false}, {"text": "65°", "added": false}, {"text": "54°", "added": false}, {"text": "35°", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 20, "text": "The cost of 21 pencils and 9 pens is ₹276, and the cost of 6 pencils and 3 pens is ₹84. The cost of 1 pencil and 1 pen is:", "options": [{"text": "₹20", "added": false}, {"text": "₹10", "added": false}, {"text": "₹40", "added": false}, {"text": "₹30", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 21, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "30°", "added": false}, {"text": "75°", "added": false}, {"text": "60°", "added": false}, {"text": "45°", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 22, "text": "A public library has an average attendance of 410 on Sundays and 230 for the remaining days. The average attendance per day of a month of 30 days beginning with Sunday would be:", "options": [{"text": "230", "added": false}, {"text": "254", "added": false}, {"text": "320", "added": false}, {"text": "260", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "simple-average", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 23, "text": "Due to decrease in manpower, the production in a factory decreases by 25%. By what per cent should the working hours be increased to restore the original production?", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "successive-change", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 24, "text": "Two numbers are, respectively, 30% and 40% more than the third number. The ratio of the second number to the first number is:", "options": [{"text": "26:28", "added": false}, {"text": "14:13", "added": false}, {"text": "39:42", "added": false}, {"text": "13:14", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "increase-decrease", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 25, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}]}